::GEO_U04_L05_Q11::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U04_L05_Q11<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>Readiness Support Only<br><br>Question:<br>A right triangle has hypotenuse 5 and one leg 3. What is the other leg? {
~A. 2#Subtracting side lengths ignores the squared relationship.
~B. 8#Adding the known lengths does not find a missing leg.
=C. 4#Use b<sup>2</sup> = 5<sup>2</sup> - 3<sup>2</sup>; the missing leg is 4.
~D. &radic;34#Adding squares would be used if both known sides were legs, but 5 is the hypotenuse.
}

